<title>UK: Bulker still aground at Saudi port with barley.</title>
<headline>Bulker still aground at Saudi port with barley.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulk carrier Qena is still aground at the Saudi Arabian port of Dammam with a cargo of bulk barley, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Salvors commenced transferring part of the 33,987 tonne cargo on February 2 after unsuccessful attempts to refloat the vessel. A further attempt may be made on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Egyptian-flag 38,319 dwt Qena went aground on January 27.</p>
<p>It is apparently aground on soft mud/sand and there is no indication of water ingress, Lloyds said.</p>
</text>
